Sequence Diagram
Here we have to reprsent how two classes communicate
-When a user performs an action, which object talks to which object, and in what sequence, to represent this we use Sequence Diagram.

A Sequence Diagram is a UML behavioral diagram that illustrates how objects interact with each other in a specific scenario by showing the sequence of method calls over time. 
It helps visualize the flow of execution for a use case.

Driver     EntranceGate     ParkingLot      ParkingSpot     Ticket
   |              |               |               |            |
   | Enter()      |               |               |            |
   |------------->|               |               |            |
   |              | findSpot()    |               |            |
   |              |-------------->|               |            |
   |              |               | assignSpot()  |            |
   |              |               |-------------> |            |
   |              |               | <-------------|            |
   |              | createTicket()|               |            |
   |              |------------------------------------------->|
   |              |<-------------------------------------------|
   |<-------------|               |               |            |

Flow
Driver arrives.
Entrance Gate asks Parking Lot for an available spot.
Parking Lot assigns a parking spot.
Entrance Gate creates a ticket.
Ticket is returned to the driver.

Components of a Sequence Diagram
1. Actor
The external user or system.
User

2. Object (Lifeline)
Represents an object participating in the interaction.
User      LoginService      Database

3. Lifeline
The vertical dashed line showing the object's existence over time.
LoginService
     |
     |
     |

4. Message
An arrow representing a method call.
LoginUI ---- validate() ----> LoginService

5. Return Message
Shows the response.
Database <---- User Details ---- LoginService
